# Security Review Required

- For authentication logic, database writes, and any user-controlled input, include a `<SECURITY_REVIEW>` section in proposals and implementations.
- `<SECURITY_REVIEW>` must include:
  - Vulnerability audit (XSS, CSRF, SQL injection, auth bypass, sensitive data exposure),
  - Mitigations applied,
  - Verification test case.
- Enforce runtime input validation with Zod (or existing project equivalent) at trust boundaries (actions, handlers, middleware, webhooks).
- Use parameterized queries/ORM protections; never build SQL strings from raw user input.
- Keep auth/session checks on the server side; validate cookies/headers defensively and fail closed on invalid state.
- Sanitize or safely render user-supplied content; avoid `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` unless strongly justified and sanitized.
- Align recommendations with OWASP and official Next.js security guidance.
